Every clinician should obtain a buprenorphine-prescribing-waiver for an opioid-use-disorder-treatment.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid in a community and the community does not have a sufficient-opioid-use-disorder-treatment-capacity then the clinician should particularly obtain a buprenorphine-prescribing-waiver for an opioid-use-disorder-treatment.
If a clinician does not provably have a buprenorphine-prescribing-waiver then it is recommended that the clinician does not prescribe a buprenorphine-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder.
